//! Files in the project, read when called — bind them at the top level, not in
//! `draw`. Paths are relative to the entry file's folder and must stay inside
//! the project. Desktop, `functor export`, and Quest (`functor run vr` pushes
//! the project's files first); not the web yet.
//!
//! Data you don't ship (game files the player owns) goes under an external
//! prefix. `functor.json` declares it: `"external": {"ss2/": "player SS2
//! data"}`. An uncommitted `functor.local.json` beside it maps it on this
//! machine to a folder or into a zip: `{"external": {"ss2/":
//! "~/ss2/sshock2.kpf!data/res/"}}`. Then `File.bytes("ss2/mesh/x.bin")` reads
//! `data/res/mesh/x.bin` in the archive, case-sensitively. External folders are
//! never pushed or bundled.

/// The bytes of a file: `File.bytes("data/model.bin")`.
let bytes : (string) => Bytes.t
/// Whether the project has the file — e.g. to fall back when an optional,
/// uncommitted input (a game asset) isn't there.
let exists : (string) => bool
